 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the real property actions and proceedings law, in relation to\nrequiring loan services for loans on vacant and abandoned residential real\nproperty to pay certain condominium common charges",
    "basePrintNo": "S7479",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7479-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1308, RPAP L",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Actions and Proceedings Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7479\n\nSPONSOR: REICHLIN-MELNICK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the real property actions and proceedings law, in\nrelation to requiring loan services for loans on vacant and abandoned\nresidential real property to pay certain condominium common charges\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would clarify that loan servicers must pay the common charges\nfor vacant and abandoned condominiums.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill amends section 1308 of the real property actions\nand proceedings law as it relates to including common charges for vacant\nand abandoned condominiums to the list of required obligations by loan\nservicers.\n\nSection two of the bill relates to the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill will clarify that loan servicers must pay for the common\ncharges for vacant and abandoned properties. The non-payment of common\ncharges for units that are vacant and abandoned places significant\nfiscal strain on condo associations that must continue to provide the\nsame services with less revenue. The burden often falls on other condo\nassociation unit owners through special assessments to account for loss\nrevenue.\n\nIn 2019, New York State adopted a new law that required loan servicers\nto pay for the homeowners associations and cooperative fees for vacant\nand abandoned properties. The intent of the original law was to include\ncondominiums associations but did not explicitly state that loan servi-\ncers are required to pay for common charges of condominiums.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
